{
  "_comment": [
    "The app-icon badge is drawn by TWO writers: the page (notify/appbadge.ts, over",
    "the visit store) and the service worker (sw.js, over the named set in the push",
    "payload built by tmux-api/pushsender.go). Nothing pinned them to the same",
    "arithmetic, and they disagreed in production: the server counted every finished",
    "session, the page counted only the unread ones, so any push reset the icon",
    "upward. This fixture is read by BOTH test suites and both must reach `want`.",
    "",
    "`visits[name]` is when the user last looked at that session; `states[name].at`",
    "is when it reached its current state. Read AFTER it finished means seen.",
    "Both sides derive the seen set that way rather than being handed it.",
    "Every session carries owner:'wizard' because /sessions stamps owner on your own sessions too. An earlier fixture left it out, which let a counter that excluded any session with an owner pass while drawing zero in production."
  ],
